nly the DNS payload', 'description': 'Message has no TSIG set (tsigState == TSIG_UNSIGNED). toWire should serialize the message normally and not append any TSIG trailer.'}]}, {'group': 'TSIG handling – signed message', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'maxLength', 'value': 1500}], 'expected': 'byte[] that ends with a TSIGRecord and whose total length does not exceed maxLength', 'description': 'Message is signed by calling setTSIG(key). The internal tsigState becomes TSIG_SIGNED. toWire must append the TSIG RR at the end of the wire format. The test verifies that the last 10‑+ bytes correspond to a TSIG RR and that the overall length respects the supplied maxLength.'}]}, {'group': 'TSIG handling – intermediate state (partial signing)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'maxLength', 'value': 1500}], 'expected': 'IllegalStateException', 'description': 'Message has tsigState == TSIG_INTERMEDIATE (e.g., after calling toWire(out) once but before final signing). Attempting a second toWire(maxLength) should fail because the message is in an inconsistent state.'}]}, {'group': 'Error conditions – null maxLength (negative value)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'maxLength', 'value': -1}], 'expected': 'IllegalArgumentException', 'description': 'Passing a negative maxLength is illegal; the method should immediately throw an IllegalArgumentException before attempting any serialization.'}]}, {'group': 'Error conditions – message with malformed header', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'maxLength', 'value': 512}], 'expected': 'IOException', 'description': 'Header fields (e.g., opcode, rcode) are set to values that are not permitted by the DNS spec. During serialization the method should raise an IOException indicating an invalid header.'}]}, {'group': 'Boundary condition – maxLength exactly required size', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'maxLength', 'value': 'wireSize'}], 'expected': 'byte[] whose length equals wireSize and matches the output of toWire() without a maxL